                            <div class="full_record_data_value">
                                Portrait of Johannes Kepler, engraved by Jakob van der Heyden. <br><br>Johannes Kepler (1571-1630) was a German mathematician and astronomer/astrologer. He worked for Tycho Brahe and was an advisor to Emperor Rudolf II. <br><br>From a set of albums known as Collectanea Newtoniana, a selection of prints, original artwork and manuscripts relating to Newton, collected by Charles Turnor (1768-1853). Turnor was an astronomer, collector and Fellow of the Royal Society. He owned Woolsthorpe Manor (Newton’s birthplace).<br>
                            </div>
                            
                        
                            
                            
